        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1354">

                <pb facs="1330" n="1320" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/8–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McConaughy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-26T18:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1720. Re third para urtel 3412 Aug 24 rptd Nanking 1826 Canton 1035. Pls impress
                    APL agent desirability receiving definite assurances from Commie auths covering
                    every possible point of controversy <pb facs="1331" n="1321" xml:id="pg1321"/>
                    that can be foreseen in entry exit <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi> Shanghai
                    (this preferably be done only if [and] when entry ship assured). This not only
                    desirable for safety passengers and vessel, but for prevention any incident
                    having polit implications, which might be serious. We also suggest APL or others
                    who handle rice imports have clear understanding with Commie auths re
                    consignees, import duty, etc.</p>
                <p>Although APL wld desire transport some off-loaded cargo from Hong Kong, no
                    commitment shld be given Commies this score. Pls note from Cantel 991 Aug 19
                    rptd Shanghai 507 Nats will not approve outward cargo Shanghai. APL also
                    desirous book about 600 Chi en route Shanghai previously off-loaded Hong Kong;
                    we have informed APL our own chief interest is travel Amers and to extent
                    possible other foreigners who wish leave Shanghai and that question travel Chi,
                    if their transport desired, cld be taken up directly with Natl Govt by APL, but
                    shld not become obstruction to project. APL here appears agreeable this line
                    action.</p>
                <p>Re ur 3341 Aug 19, Dept proposes inform Nats through Canton and Taipei precise
                    itinerary, markings, etc., <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi> at appropriate
                    time for info Natlst mil units.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
